ver  some of these cities  we are able to see the name of the city  and the population associated with it  something else we can do with the scalar  associate  values associated with our locations is  not just to plot them as points and  color them by their value but also to  increase the size so that the size  represents the different  um scalar values so we have a plot that  does this which is bubble chart  and so um the corresponding plot that we  have  for geo visualization is geo bubble  chart and so for the same  data we can see now that  the bubbles corresponding to the capital  city locations  reflect the population size of that city  so we also get to inherit all the  features of bubble chart here so if i  hover over some of these bubbles you can  see  that you have a mouse over effect and  you get a tooltip  that tells you the scalar value that is  associated with that position  something else we can do is to  interpolate the scalar values  so we have different scalar values  associated with  the capital cities and we can  interpolate the populations  and we can overlay the interpolated  graphic on top of the geographics so  that corresponds to those locations  and so we use this density plot to  get the interpolated density and then  we plot it at the locations so the plot  is called geodensity plot  and here i would like to draw your  attention to  a region function which is able to  specify  europe as the area that is  that you want to clip the density to and  so you get a nice clipping of the  the density around around europe  so here is a an example of how  different options for the geographics  and  visualization functions work together so  here we have  on the right hand side of the rule  we have the elevation data for the  different capital cities of europe  and so an actual way that we want to be  able to plot them  is to use the contours  and so we have geocontour plot which  plots the contour values  based on the elevation data for the  capital 