anations there  and finally here is the specification  that  associate weights with the locations so  that we can get the  intensity of the locations and so here  we have  a histogram where the locations of the  capital cities  are weighted by their city populations  and so  we get a  [Music]  histogram a geohistogram where the bins  are located  at the position at the locations  and we have the bins that tell us how  many  how much population falls into each of  these bins  here we have geo smooth histogram which  takes the data and i just have the data  in a different format here but  slightly different data for capital  cities of the eurozone countries  and their corresponding populations  and so that's what the data looks like  and if we fit it  into geosmooth histogram then we get the  kernel  kernel density of the locations  weighted by their populations and then  we can overlay that on top of  the geographics  so the last class of data that we  looked at was vector values at locations  and so um let's begin by constructing  a geo vector and  we just pick 100 random locations  uh in the world and we associate  each of those locations with a vector  value  we can of course plot this directly  using geographics in the geomarker  and each of those vectors are plotted as  an arrow and  using geographics and we can set the  geoprotection  etc but if we wanted to  discern some pattern um in the in the  vectors what we  use is a geovector plot which then takes  the  array of those vectors and plots the  vector field and so here we have  the direction of the arrows showing the  direction of the  vector field and the color of the arrows  represents the magnitude of the vector  field at that position  and this is uh something that we changed  recently  for a vector plot where which moved away  from  using the size of the arrows to  represent the magnitude of the vector  field to using color  and so that's something that we can  directly inherit into a geo vector plot  and and use it there  another example where we're using the  updated  vector markers so here we have  markers that are shaped like water drops  and um and again this is something that  we updated for  vector plot and we're able to use it in  geovector plot  we can also visualize streamlines  using geostream plot and this is again  based on  stream plots and we're able to use  stream style  to set the thickness of the streamlines  and geo background to change  the look of the underlying geographic so  this gives you some idea of the  flexibility  of of geo visualizations and the  approach that we take  to unify the options for geographics and  geographizations  and finally i just want to end with  the new features and updates that we  have added to  geo visualizations and  you have already looked at some of these  um  in the examples about i just wanted to  point them out to you  so this one um the original value plot  um here is plotting  the countries of europe and covering  them by their population  but what happens is sometimes some of  the countries in plots like this  they are at a different scale than than  the other countries here so  it becomes sometimes difficult to  um discern the  the polygons that represent the smaller  countries  from the ones that are much bigger  and so one of the features that we've  added is for geo  region value plot to auto identify the  scale difference  and to highlight  the smaller features in  in visualization using points for  example  so here it's able to auto identify the  countries that might  have much smaller polygons than the  others and  it positions a point at those locations  another feature that we're adding is the  ability to  segment colors and so for geo region  value plot  here in this case when we are plotting  the locations of the capital cities and  coloring them by their population  in addition to being able to specify the  color scheme  to be used it makes sense to  be able to specify the method to be used  to to classify the values to split the  values into different classes  so that we get nice visual separation in  terms of the colors that are being used  and so the mechanism that we use for  that is  color function which is a list here  and the first part of the call function  takes the  the color scheme to be used and the the  second  part of the list specifies the method  that is to be used to classify  the scalar values and so we're using  k-means as a method here and  and that is a quantile based method  that can be used to create more  separation in terms of colors  and finally we have  updated a couple of parsers for  for gls plot and geo region value plot  and so  we are able to more consistently handle  the data for these plots  this enables us to  be able to support a wider range of  primitives than before and virtually  almost all the primitives that are  handled by  geographics directly and so you'll be  able to  for example plot geodesics and  other primitives directly into geolist  plot  and create custom  geoplots this also  puts us in a better position to  be able to support new and updated  features coming down the pike  not just from geographics in terms of  updated geoprimitives  but also new areas in the language like  spatial  statistics which is a a big area  that we're going to have features in  and we want to be able to visualize some  of those  in geoplots and  i guess that brings us uh to the end of  my talk  and um i will stop here and thank you  very much for attending and i'll see  if there are any questions in the chat i  will take them now  thank you okay so  let me take a quick look at the  questions here  i think uh most of them have already  been answered by  brett and emmanuel so let's see um  the possible to include legends of  bubble sizes that's been answered by  brett  um phil  ramston bratislava yes that's that's  correct rihanna and bratislava  are a position almost um  they're on the same bin there so  okay so  which geographic's functionalities are  new in 12.2  um  so so for 12.2 like i said in the  in the presentation and there's been a  big update to  geo list blood and geo region by iu plot  so we can  we can have more support for  different data types that can be handled  more consistently  um but then we also have um  updates to how the color is segmented  which is a big  big piece of work that emanuel did um  so i guess no new plots per se in 12.2  but in 12.1 we added  some of the um some of the new plots  um and brett said we've been  consistently adding  new um visualization visualizations uh  for every version since nine  okay any more questions  i don't see any in the chat for zoom  either  okay so i'll just end it here thank you  you
 

